// A marker, never compiled: a module in a directory that also holds core.grl is a standard-library
// module (in_std_dir), and only the standard library may write an inherent impl for a built-in type
// (`impl u64 { ... }`, `impl<T> T[] { ... }`). The corpus cases whose files live here exercise that
// machinery directly instead of through lib/'s own impls.
module core;
